<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Shell unit to build $51 mln plant.</title>
<headline>Argentine Shell unit to build $51 mln plant.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Capsa, the Argentine unit of the Dutch oil giant, said Monday it will invest $51.6 million to build a plant for water treatment of diesel at its refinary at Dock Sud, in Buenos Aires.</p>
<p>&quot;The diesel that will be produced at the future plant will substitute the diesel that has to be imported now to satisfy growing domestic demand,&quot; said Shell in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant, which will be built by ABB Lummus Global, is expected to be operative at the beginning of 1998.</p>
<p>The plant is part of a previously-announced five-year $600 million investment program by Shell Capsa.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Adam, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180654</p>
